				<div class="entry">
					<p>Birth Date: January 12, 1953                                     URS date: August 2, 2011</p>
<h5 id="dspDetail_byLine" title="2011-08-24T00:00:00Z">August 24, 2011</h5>
<div id="attachment_876" style="width: 209px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><a href="wp-content/uploads/2011/11/Shambu-Charles-Mardel-wreath.jpeg"><img class="size-full wp-image-876" title="Shambu Charles Mardel wreath" src="wp-content/uploads/2011/11/Shambu-Charles-Mardel-wreath.jpeg" alt="" width="199" height="199" /></a><p class="wp-caption-text">I find ecstasy in living -- the mere sense of living is joy enough. Emily Dickinson</p></div>
<div>The Maui News</div>
<p>Our dearly beloved brother, Charles &#8220;Shambu&#8221; Mardel, died on August 2, 2011 at his home in Kamaole.</p>
<p>Private services were held by the family on Maui.</p>
<p>Shambu was born on Jan. 12, 1953 in Buffalo, N.Y. to Alfred and Florine Mardel.</p>
<p>He was a Chinese herbalist, acupuncturist, and healer.</p>
<p>He is survived by his wife, Claudia Mardel; sister, Christine Thomas of CA; brother, Frank Mardel.</p>
<p>Shambu was loved and cherished by many people across the world and we joyously commit his soul to God</p>
<p><a href="wp-content/uploads/2011/11/Shambu-the-accupuncturist.jpg"><img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-879" title="Shambu the accupuncturist" src="wp-content/uploads/2011/11/Shambu-the-accupuncturist.jpg" alt="Shambu Charles Mardel practicing Acupuncture for over 20 years.  A very gifted healer and friend to all." width="180" height="120" /></a></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Shambu <strong>Charles Mardel</strong> practicing Acupuncture for over 20 years.</p>
<p>A very gifted healer and friend to all.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
	
				       				
																					
				</div>
		
				<p class="postmetadata"><a href="index.html?p=874#comments" title="Comment on Shambu Charles Mardel">1 Comment &#187;</a></p>
				
<!-- You can start editing here. -->

	<h3 id="comments">One Memory for &#8220;Shambu Charles Mardel&#8221;</h3> 

	<ol class="commentlist">
						<li class="alt" id="comment-12520">
			<div class="cmtinfo"><em> on 03 Aug 2012 at 5:09 am</em><small class="commentmetadata"><a href="index.html?p=874#comment-12520" title=""><span class="commentnum">1</span></a></small><cite><a href='http://Aguadeflora.com' rel='external nofollow' class='url'>Ryan Hornback</a></cite></div>
						
			<p>One year today my friend Charles (Shambu)  left his body to the earth. Having known this beautiful man I can only imagine his current state of  consciousness.  Charles was not only an excellent  acupuncturist, but a true healer, there are many of the former but few of the latter. To  have both in one person is truly a blessing. He was a healer of the highest order, with an awesome ability to sense the source of life, in a heartbeat.   &#8220;May all beings be happy&#8221;</p>
<p>                   Thank you Shambu.            your friend Ryan-</p>
			
		</li>

	
	
	</ol>

